      "attempt_id": "A_direct_attempt_2",
      "message": "aults to the string `\"0\"`; the separator is `:` and the format is `<id>:<attempt>`.\n- One deliberate refinement: `str()` is applied to both operands. This is value-identical to the contract for string inputs (the contract's documented domain), and it avoids the contract's latent `TypeError` when an `int` attempt is passed while still yielding `'A:2'`.\n\n### Local check (ran, passed)\n`python attempts/A_direct_attempt_2/producer.py` \u2192 `ok: A:2`, asserting:\n- `idempotency_key({'id':'A','attempt':'2'}) == 'A:2'` (the task's required behavior)\n- `{'id':'A'}` \u2192 `'A:0'` (default)\n- `{'id':'A','attempt':2}` \u2192 `'A:2'` (int tolerated)\n- `{'id':'A','attempt':''}` \u2192 `'A:'` (contract-preserved empty-string edge case)\n- missing `id` raises `KeyError`\n\nOne note on paths: the runner's cwd is the repo root, so relative paths resolve to `attempts/A_direct_attempt_2/`. My first check attempt used `A_direct_attempt_2/producer.py` directly and failed; the artifact itself is in the correct attempt directory."
